I agree with that (and from my own experience, most people do
hold on to their genocide scrolls until they can bless them.)
But there's at least two cases in vanilla where it makes sense 
to read genocide uncursed:

- To get rid of specific monsters without eliminating the rest
  of the class -- notably (master) mind flayers and minotaurs,
  and I'm sure there's more.
- As a emergency action to eliminate a monster that's
  currently a danger to you.

With either suggestion (or the UnNethack solution), I think
the first goes away -- blessed genocide is strictly better
than uncursed.  I'm sure there are some oddball cases where
it still might make sense to prefer an uncursed scroll, but
that's going to be rare.  But if you introduce a failure
chance, then the second possibility is no longer viable either
unless the player is thoroughly spoiled (and so knows the
formula), or is doing it as a last-ditch resort hoping for a
good result (which is on par with blind-reading scrolls and
so forth.)

